FF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-s2/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make plan approval one atomic publication boundary[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]archive-ownership[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]archive-ownership: establish one host-owned canonical plan archive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]operation, publish its durable path in the terminal gate response before[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a planner can resume, retain an explicit compatibility fallback for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]genuinely old responses, and prove that concurrent approval and runner [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]writers cannot recur.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Hold approved epic launches through developer source swaps[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]swap-safe-epic-launch[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]swap-safe-epic-launch: keep direct bead work fail-fast while making the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]detached host-owned epic launcher wait outside the editable SASE import [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]boundary, then execute exactly once from a fresh process under the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]existing code-swap reader protection.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prove the combined approval-to-launch lifecycle[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]reliability-integration[dim] · [dim][/dim]after archive-ownership, swap-safe-epic-launch[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reliability-integration: exercise tale approval, sidecar link [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]finalization, epic approval during a developer update, and exhaustive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repository checks together so neither fix